2406:         // One placement step for a defense. Candidate spots are sampled around our buildings with a free power slot
2407:         // (the game's connector ring, capped at the defense radius). Every candidate goes through the game's own full
2408:         // placement check (TryPlaceBuilding: terrain, collisions, fallout; it places nothing) and the game's exact
2409:         // power-line rule (PlayerPowerGridHandler: centre distance <= both radii + the longer connector range); the legal
2410:         // one covering the most uncovered value wins. With nothing left to cover the same safe path places it anywhere
2411:         // legal and connected: we never hand a defense back to the game's search, which samples past line reach
2412:         // (Terra v0.7.1). No legal spot this step -> try again next step; the abandon valve refunds a hopeless search.
2413:         // Defense searches fail closed (Terra v0.7.2): on an error, a missing radius or too many fruitless steps the search
2414:         // is pushed to the abandon valve (refund) instead of the game's own search, which can leave the defense unconnected.
2415:         private static void AbandonSoon(AIBuildingPlacementSearch search)
2416:         {
2417:             s_searchSteps.SetValue(search, Math.Max((int)s_searchSteps.GetValue(search), Math.Max(100, Plugin.PlacementStepCap.Value)));
